<title>USA: St Joseph hogs off $0.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs off $0.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Wednesday, barrows and gilts were $0.50 lower. Top $57.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>Too wet to plow so they took hogs to town. Interior Iowa moved 111,000 Wednesday. However, packers cut their kills this week and not needing as many hogs.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    230-270 lbs	57.00-57.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-290 lbs	55.50-56.50</p>
<p>Sows - scarce.</p>
<p>Boars - scarce.</p>
</text>
